1. what is a tree data structure ?
Solution: a tree is a non-linear data structure used to store data in a hierarchical manner. 
think about a family tree or the folder structure on your computer.

For example:

                a 
               / \
              b   c
            /  \  
            d   e
              / / \
              f g h 

consider this tree:

                          10
                         /  \
                        20  30
                       / \   /
                      40 50  60

here, 

10 is the root node
20 and 30 are children of 10
10 is the parent of 20 and 30
40, 50 and 60 are leaf nodes
the connection between two nodes is called an edge.

